* SETEXIT FACE 7 -- THE TRAP, MEASURED ON AN ERROR SCRIP ACTUALLY RAISES.
* se_trap_fires uses 1/D, which SCRIP does not raise at all (it silently degrades the error to
* statement failure), so that witness cannot separate a missing TRAP from a missing RAISE.
* An undefined function call raises in both engines, so this row isolates the trap.
* The handler prints a BARE MARKER on purpose.  &ERRTEXT is worded differently by the two
* engines and &LASTNO needs the statement counter, which does not advance in this tree
* (g_core_err_stmt, seat8 s194) -- both are their own rungs and se_trap_lastno tracks them.
	SETEXIT(.H)
	&ERRLIMIT = 10
	X = NOSUCHFN(1)
	OUTPUT = "AFTER"
	:(END)
H	OUTPUT = "HANDLER"
	:(END)
END
